---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: collections.essayPages
  size: 1
  alias: essay
permalink: "/e/{{ essay.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ essay.title }}"
---
<article class="post essay-page">
  {#- The essay's date seeds the same day-sky a daily gets, so the essay and
      the daily it shipped alongside share a band. Before this the header kept
      the daily's padding with nothing drawn in it — 3.3rem of air under the
      date (2026-09-06). -#}
  <header class="post-head" style="--day-sky:url({{ essay.date | daySky }})">
    <h1 class="post-title">{{ essay.title }}</h1>
    <p class="post-subdate">{{ essay.date | readableDate }}</p>
  </header>
  {#- One shelf card per cited subject. SPANs inside, same reason as the
      shelf: the card is one anchor. A card whose subject a ## heading names
      goes under that heading (essay.sections, config); the rest float beside
      the opening paragraph — the essay's one guaranteed image. -#}
  {% macro card(c) %}
  <a class="essay-card shelf-card{% if c.canon %} is-canon{% elif c.rating and c.rating.slug == "favorite" %} is-favorite{% endif %}" href="/s/{{ c.slug }}/">
    <span class="shelf-art">
      {% if c.coverUrl %}
      <img class="shelf-cover" src="{{ c.coverUrl }}" alt="{{ c.title }} cover art" decoding="async">
      {% else %}
      <span class="sky" style="background-image:url({{ c.skyUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {% endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="cell badge b-{{ c.status }}">{{ c.status }}</span>
    {% if c.canon %}<span class="cell rating badge-g b-canon" data-g="♥">canon</span>
    {% elif c.rating %}<span class="cell rating r-{{ c.rating.slug }}">{{ c.rating.title }}</span>
    {% else %}<span class="cell rating r-pending">pending</span>{% endif %}
  </a>
  {% endmacro %}
  {% for c in essay.topCards %}{{ card(c) }}{% endfor %}
  {% for s in essay.sections %}
  <section class="essay-section">
    {{ s.head | safe }}
    {% if s.card %}{{ card(s.card) }}{% endif %}
    {{ s.body | safe }}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
  {#- The essay mirror of a daily's tag footer: the subjects it's about
      (about-list order), then the union of their tags plus any tag cited
      directly (tagviews order). Every view this essay appears in, linked. -#}
  {% if (essay.cites | length) or (essay.citedTags | length) %}
  <p class="tag-list post-tags">
    {% for c in essay.cites %}<a class="tag-link" href="/s/{{ c.slug }}/">{{ c.title }}</a>{% endfor %}
    {% for t in essay.citedTags %}<a class="tag-link" href="/t/{{ t.slug }}/">#{{ t.slug }}</a>{% endfor %}
  </p>
  {% endif %}
</article>
